  "question": {
    "text": "In the circuit shown below, the ac source has voltage $V=20 \\cos (\\omega t)$ volt with $\\omega=2000 \\mathrm{rad} / \\mathrm{s}$\r\n\r\nThe amplitude of the current will be nearest to\r\n\r\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0010_61795ae588a2.png\">"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$3.3 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$2 / \\sqrt{5} \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{5} \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\r\nZ=& \\sqrt{R^{2}+\\left(\\omega L-\\frac{1}{\\omega C}\\right)^{2}} \\\\\r\n\r\n&=\\sqrt{10^{2}+\\left(2000 \\times 5 \\times 10^{3}-\\frac{1}{2000 \\times 50 \\times 10^{-6}}\\right)^{2}} \\\\\r\n\r\n=& 10 \\Omega \\\\\r\n\r\n\\quad i=\\frac{V_{0}}{Z}=\\frac{20}{10}=2 A .\r\n\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n\r\n$$"
  }
